    "final_answer": "I have completed the task by comparing the iPhone 14 Pro and iPhone 15 Pro from Apple's website. Here is the comparison:\n\n## iPhone 14 Pro vs iPhone 15 Pro — Comparison from Apple.com\n\n| Feature | iPhone 14 Pro | iPhone 15 Pro |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Chip** | A16 Bionic chip | A17 Pro chip |\n| **Price** | Available at authorized resellers | Available at authorized resellers |\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**Chips:**\n- **iPhone 14 Pro** is powered by the **A16 Bionic chip** (6-core CPU, 5-core GPU, 16-core Neural Engine)\n- **iPhone 15 Pro** is powered by the **A17 Pro chip** (6-core CPU, 6-core GPU, 16-core Neural Engine, plus hardware-accelerated ray tracing — an upgrade from the iPhone 14 Pro)\n\n**Prices:**\n- Neither the iPhone 14 Pro nor the iPhone 15 Pro is currently sold directly on Apple's website. Both models are listed as **\"Available at authorized resellers\"** — meaning Apple has discontinued direct sales of these older Pro models (they are now only available through third-party retailers).\n- The current iPhone lineup on Apple's website features newer models like the iPhone 18 Pro, iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone Air, and iPhone 16 Pro.\n\n### Summary:\nThe most notable difference between these two models is the **chip upgrade** from the A16 Bionic to the A17 Pro (which introduced hardware-accelerated ray tracing and an extra GPU core). Both phones were originally priced starting at $999 when launched, but their current purchase price must be obtained through authorized resellers since Apple no longer sells them directly.\n\nSource: [Apple iPhone Compare page](https://www.apple.com/iphone/compare/?modelList=iphone-14-pro,iphone-15-pro,iphone-18-pro) (captured 2026-09-17)",
